================================================================
  musil: library reference (scientific)
================================================================

--- construction ---
a literal       : ((1 2) (3 4))
list->mat       : ((1 2) (3 4))
mat-zeros 2 3   : ((0 0 0) (0 0 0))
mat-ones 1 2    : ((1 1))
mat-fill 2 2 7  : ((7 7) (7 7))
eye 3           : ((1 0 0) (0 1 0) (0 0 1))
diag (vec 2 3)  : ((2 0) (0 3))
col-stack       : ((1 4) (2 5) (3 6)) (the vectors become columns)

--- shape and access ---
nrows, ncols    : 3 3   mat-shape: (3 3)
mat-get M 1 2   : 6
mat-row M 0     : (1 2 3)
mat-col M 2     : (3 6 10)
mat-diag M      : (1 5 10)
get-rows M 1 2  : ((4 5 6) (7 8 10)) (2 rows from row 1)
get-cols M 0 2  : ((1 2) (4 5) (7 8)) (2 columns from column 0)
mat-set in place: ((0 9) (0 0))

--- elementwise and stacking ---
mat-add A B     : ((6 8) (10 12))
mat-sub B A     : ((4 4) (4 4))
hadamard A B    : ((5 12) (21 32))
mat-scale A 3   : ((3 6) (9 12))
mat-shift A 10  : ((11 12) (13 14))
mat-map A sqrt  : ((1 1.4142135623731) (1.73205080756888 2))
vstack A B      : ((1 2) (3 4) (5 6) (7 8))
hstack A B      : ((1 2 5 6) (3 4 7 8))

--- products and decompositions ---
mat-mul A B     : ((19 22) (43 50))
mat-mul A B A   : ((85 126) (193 286)) (left to right)
mat-vec A (1 1) : (3 7)
vec-mat (1 1) A : (4 6)
outer (1 2) (3 4): ((3 4) (6 8))
trace M         : 16
transpose M     : ((1 4 7) (2 5 8) (3 6 10))
det A, det M    : -2 -3
rank M          : 3   rank of (1 2; 2 4): 1
inv A           : ((-2 1) (1.5 -0.5))
A inv(A)        : ((1 0) (0 1))
solve A (5 11)  : (1 2)
singular        : reference_scientific.mu:74: inv: matrix is singular
not square      : reference_scientific.mu:75: det: matrix must be square (1x3)
ragged          : reference_scientific.mu:76: transpose: ragged matrix: row 1 has 1 columns, expected 2
eig-sym         : ((3 1) ((0.707106781186547 0.707106781186547) (0.707106781186547 -0.707106781186547))) (eigenvalues, then eigenvectors as rows)
A v = lambda v  : (2.12132034355964 2.12132034355964) = (2.12132034355964 2.12132034355964)

--- statistics ---
median-filter 3 : (1 1 1 1 1 1 1 1) (spikes removed; median itself is in std)
linefit         : (2 1) (slope intercept)
lp-norm 1, 2, 3 : 7 5 4.4979
dist, dist-p 1  : 5 7
dist-matrix     : ((0 5 10) (5 0 5) (10 5 0))
nearest         : 1
center          : ((-1 -5) (1 5))
axis 0 is down the columns, axis 1 along the rows:
mat-sum  0, 1   : (12 15 19) (6 15 25)
mat-mean 0, 1   : (4 5 6.33333333333333) (2 5 8.33333333333333)
mat-std  0, 1   : (2.449 2.449 2.867) (0.816 0.816 1.247)
zscore          : ((-1.225 -1.225 -1.162) (0 0 -0.116) (1.225 1.225 1.279))
cov             : ((9 9 10.5) (9 9 10.5) (10.5 10.5 12.333))
corr            : ((1 1 0.997) (1 1 0.997) (0.997 0.997 1))

--- regression ---
design matrix   : ((1 0) (1 1) (1 2) (1 3))
linreg-fit      : (1 2) (intercept slope)
linreg-predict  : (1 3 5 7)
residuals       : (0 0 0 0)

--- pca ---
pca             : ((0.9998 -0.0201 2.501) (0.0201 0.9998 0.009)) (each row: direction then its eigenvalue, largest first)
pca-directions  : ((0.9998 -0.0201) (0.0201 0.9998))
pca-eigenvalues : (2.501 0.009)
pca-explained   : (0.9964 0.0036)
pca-scores 1    : (0.9978 2.0016 2.9974 4.0012 4.999)

--- kmeans ---
kmeans-labels   : (0 0 0 1 1 1)
kmeans-centroids: ((0.033 0.033) (10.033 10.033))
cluster-sizes   : (3 3)

--- knn ---
knn             : (a b)
knn-predict-one : b
knn-test        : (a a b b)
accuracy        : 1
train-test-split: (2 2) (after shuffle)

--- display ---
mat-str M 2:
 1.00   2.00   3.00
 4.00   5.00   6.00
 7.00   8.00  10.00
mat-print (inv A):
-2.000   1.000
 1.500  -0.500
mat-print-with (cov M) 1:
 9.0   9.0  10.5
 9.0   9.0  10.5
10.5  10.5  12.3

================================================================
  end of scientific reference
